# Normalise line endings in the repository.
* text=auto

# Keep Go sources as LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# gofmt always emits LF. On a Windows checkout with core.autocrlf=true, every
# .go file lands as CRLF, so `gofmt -l .` lists the entire tree and stops being
# a usable signal — a real formatting problem hides among dozens of false ones.
# That is exactly how a misaligned const block reached CI. Pinning eol=lf keeps
# the local check meaningful and matching what CI runs.
*.go text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for the files that carry formatting rules of their own.
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Corpus images are binary; never transform them.
*.E01 binary
*.Ex01 binary
*.L01 binary
*.Lx01 binary
*.s01 binary
*.raw binary
